note Exercism-style exercise "space-age": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/space-age
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note age is how old someone of the given seconds is in years of planet: one Earth year is 31557600
note seconds; orbital periods in Earth years are Mercury 0.2408467, Venus 0.61519726, Earth 1.0,
note Mars 1.8808158, Jupiter 11.862615, Saturn 29.447498, Uranus 84.016846, Neptune 164.79132.
note age is -1.0 when planet is not one of these names.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/space-age
om2
text pl0 "Mercury"
text pl1 "Venus"
text pl2 "Earth"
text pl3 "Mars"
text pl4 "Jupiter"
text pl5 "Saturn"
text pl6 "Uranus"
text pl7 "Neptune"
fn same a view uchar * b view uchar * to bool
if ne len a len b
ret false
end
for i ulong len a
if ne get a i get b i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn period planet view uchar * to f64
if same planet pl0
ret 0.2408467
end
if same planet pl1
ret 0.61519726
end
if same planet pl2
ret 1.0
end
if same planet pl3
ret 1.8808158
end
if same planet pl4
ret 11.862615
end
if same planet pl5
ret 29.447498
end
if same planet pl6
ret 84.016846
end
if same planet pl7
ret 164.79132
end
ret -1.0
end
fn age planet view uchar * seconds f64 to f64
p = period planet
if lt p 0.0
ret -1.0
end
ret div div seconds 31557600.0 p
end
